{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_39SttOs2MjHdNUWzu2UwiWOw","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n3\t  \"title\": \"verdict-artifact\",\n4\t  \"description\": \"autonomous-mode.md 机件 #3 的验收工件 schema。verify 每轮必产 docs/test-reports/{BL-id}-verdict.json，喂沉淀引擎（§8.4）。存在≠真实：每 feature 的 evidence / steps_to_reproduce 必须非空，机械拒收空壳 PASS。v1.1 起兼作 dispatch-mode.md 的跨厂商交付契约（deliverable.schema），并承载 waiting 中断态。\",\n5\t  \"type\": \"object\",\n6\t  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n7\t  \"required\": [\"batch_id\", \"fix_round\", \"created_at\", \"verdicts\"],\n8\t  \"properties\": {\n9\t    \"batch_id\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"= progress.json.current_sprint（BL-id）\" },\n10\t    \"fix_round\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0 },\n11\t    \"created_at\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" },\n12\t    \"waiting\": {\n13\t      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n14\t      \"enum\": [\"auth\", \"adjudication\", null],\n15\t      \"default\": null,\n16\t      \"description\": \"dispatch-mode.md 的中断态降维表达（借 A2A AUTH_REQUIRED / INPUT_REQUIRED 语义）。一次性 CLI 进程无法「挂起等你」，故把中断态编码进产物：撞 L2 边界而未获授权 → 'auth'；规格歧义 / acceptance 无法客观判定 → 'adjudication'。写完照常 exit 0——不要用非零退出码表达「我需要人」，那会被回执推断判成 FAILED 并触发无意义重派。编排者读到非空即硬停交人类。\"\n17\t    },\n18\t    \"waiting_detail\": {\n19\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n20\t      \"minLength\": 1,\n21\t      \"description\": \"waiting 非空时必填：卡在哪条 feature、需要什么授权或裁决。人类据此一眼判断如何解锁\"\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"verdicts\": {\n24\t      \"type\": \"array\",\n25\t      \"items\": {\n26\t        \"type\": \"object\",\n27\t        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n28\t        \"required\": [\"feature_id\", \"result\", \"evidence\", \"steps_to_reproduce\"],\n29\t        \"properties\": {\n30\t          \"feature_id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n31\t          \"result\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PASS\", \"PARTIAL\", \"FAIL\"] },\n32\t          \"evidence\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1, \"description\": \"实测证据（测试输出/命令/staging 结果），非空——空 = 空壳，拒收\" },\n33\t          \"steps_to_reproduce\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1 }\n34\t        }\n35\t      }\n36\t    }\n37\t  },\n38\t  \"if\": {\n39\t    \"properties\": { \"waiting\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"auth\", \"adjudication\"] } },\n40\t    \"required\": [\"waiting\"]\n41\t  },\n42\t  \"then\": {\n43\t    \"_comment\": \"中断态下允许 verdicts 为空或部分——被授权/裁决卡住时本就验不完，强行要求满额会逼出编造的证据\",\n44\t    \"required\": [\"waiting_detail\"],\n45\t    \"properties\": { \"verdicts\": { \"minItems\": 0 } }\n46\t  },\n47\t  \"else\": {\n48\t    \"_comment\": \"非中断态：verdicts 必须非空，否则这轮验收没有产出，沉淀引擎无燃料\",\n49\t    \"properties\": { \"verdicts\": { \"minItems\": 1 } }\n50\t  }\n51\t}"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_CkWSPBHBN3pBQt7jEWxGlC8U","content":"1\t# BL-REPLAY-PROCESS-BOUNDS\n2\t\n3\t## Authorization, baseline and scope\n4\t\n5\tThe user approved continuing the established risk-first order on 2026-10-08.\n6\tWork remains on the isolated takeover branch based on\n7\t`ba292a059184a36e4bb6c3341ac059606d24f961`. The preceding local privacy/queue\n8\tbatch is archived verbatim under `docs/archive/privacy-queue-closeout-20261008/`.\n9\tNo push, deployment, human gate decision, real-home source/queue access, native\n10\tservice installation, historical-data deletion or old verdict modification.\n11\t\n12\tPriority rationale: the independent B03 report on `6a030f6` identified an\n13\tunbounded module-load Git version probe (F1) and SIGTERM-ignoring children that\n14\toutlive synchronous-spawn timeouts (F2). These execution-boundary findings were\n15\tnot covered by the preceding combination evaluator's fresh derived probes.\n16\tFix them before adding privacy capabilities or the OpenCode cursor slice.\n17\tThis does not retroactively replace either prior verdict.\n18\t\n19\tThe source candidates `06f162f`, `2b8e40a`, `9aef382`, `388163c` are reference\n20\tinputs, not trusted acceptance or instructions. Selectively adapt only the\n21\tallowed changes. Do not merge other branches or change their worktrees.\n22\tThe copied report is historical evidence only: do NOT execute its real-home\n23\tqueue probe. All new fixtures must isolate HOME/USERPROFILE/TMPDIR and explicit\n24\tqueue targets before module import, and clean only their own synthetic trees.\n25\t\n26\t## F001: bounded subprocess primitive\n27\t\n28\tAllowed product paths: new `src/cli/bounded-subprocess.ts` and\n29\t`src/cli/bounded-subprocess-worker.mjs` (or one equivalent newly named helper).\n30\tAdd unit tests under `tests/cli/process-bounds/` and helper fixtures under\n31\t`tests/fixtures/process-bounds/`. No new dependencies or public protocol.\n32\t\n33\t- Provide bounded execution for an explicit executable/argument array; no shell\n34\t  command concatenation. Preserve cwd/env, ordinary exit status and signal.\n35\t- Validate finite positive timeout/output bounds before spawning. Bound combined\n36\t  stdout/stderr bytes, worker response size and cleanup time. Retain typed\n37\t  timeout/output failures; distinguish launch failure from successful output.\n38\t- A timeout, output overflow or launch error must force cleanup of the owned\n39\t  process tree, not merely send SIGTERM and wait indefinitely. POSIX uses an\n40\t  owned process group; Windows uses bounded native tree termination. Await the\n41\t  cleanup attempt before reporting completion; retain a bounded direct-child\n42\t  fallback. Do not target unrelated processes.\n43\t- Declare the worker watchdog and cleanup allowance in code/docs. Avoid claiming\n44\t  a universal hard real-time bound under suspended workers, stalled syscalls,\n45\t  deliberately escaped process groups or an unresponsive OS.\n46\t- Test normal stdout/stderr, nonzero exit, missing executable, invalid budgets,\n47\t  SIGTERM resistance, descendant inherited pipes, output overflow and no live\n48\t  owned descendants after timeout on the native platform available.\n49\t\n50\t## F002: bounded startup version snapshot\n51\t\n52\tAllowed product path: `src/cli/agent-version.ts`, using F001.\n53\tNew tests/fixtures use the directories above.\n54\t\n55\t- Preserve the startup-time SHA snapshot. Do not make it lazy or reread disk on\n56\t  later heartbeats, which would falsely identify a stale daemon as upgraded.\n57\t- Bound Git version discovery to a small explicit budget (reference: 2000 ms\n58\t  plus declared cleanup allowance), cap output, and return null on failed,\n59\t  signalled, timed-out, overflowing or invalid SHA output. No partial SHA.\n60\t- Healthy Git must still report the actual install checkout SHA; later checkout\n61\t  changes must not alter an already imported module's result.\n62\t- Run a real CLI help/status or module-import subprocess with a stalled Git\n63\t  shim under a synthetic home, measuring the startup refusal/fallback behavior.\n64\t  On Windows, fixtures must exercise an executable, not assume .cmd shell\n65\t  resolution by `execFile`/`spawn`.\n66\t\n67\t## F003: replay subprocess deadline integration\n68\t\n69\tAllowed product paths: `src/cli/git.ts`, `src/cli/replay.ts`, using F001.\n70\tNo queue/cursor/normal event identity or server changes.\n71\t\n72\t- Route deadline-bound replay Git calls and the Windows reparse-point check\n73\t  through F001. Ordinary collection behavior remains unchanged in this slice.\n74\t- Preserve one operation-wide replay deadline across reads, both enrichments,\n75\t  confirmation reread, queue-lock acquisition and before-mutate guard. Reserve\n76\t  cleanup time within the replay budget where possible; never renew the full\n77\t  timeout per Git call. Reparse validation must remain fail-closed.\n78\t- Bound output (reference: 64 KiB Git, 16 KiB reparse check). Timeout/output or\n79\t  supervision failure must refuse replay, not silently return partial enriched\n80\t  data. Ordinary missing Git/non-repository behavior remains compatible.\n81\t- Retain physical-scope checks, final payload/digest binding, source budgets,\n82\t  exact-version shared queue semantics and read-only dry-run. No diagnostic\n83\t  raw payload enters queue/network as part of this work.\n84\t- Verify preview and a valid-digest execute independently with a real resistant\n85\t  child: refused execution leaves queue/cursor/config bytes unchanged. A late\n86\t  failure between inspection and merge must still be checked under queue lock.\n87\t\n88\t## F004: regression and portable failure fixtures\n89\t\n90\tAllowed paths: new tests and fixtures under the directories above, and this\n91\tbatch's NEW generator evidence directory. No new product behavior in F004.\n92\t\n93\t- Add a baseline reproduction of the startup and SIGTERM-resistance failures\n94\t  in a disposable snapshot of `ba292a0`, with an external watchdog that cannot\n95\t  leak child processes. Do not damage or alter the frozen baseline.\n96\t- Exercise output-limit refusal and stderr canaries without exposing raw child\n97\t  output in user-visible replay errors; verify ordinary Git enrichment and\n98\t  version snapshots still work. Native-platform execution is mandatory here;\n99\t  Windows-only tests are retained with explicit macOS skips, not inferred PASS.\n100\t- Every pre-existing tracked test and report stays byte-identical to `ba292a0`.\n101\t  Do not change historical timeouts, assertions, exclusions or expected hashes.\n102\t  If an original test fails, retain the failure and seek a narrow adjudication;\n103\t  do not hide it with a new exclusion or weakened assertion.\n104\t- Record Node 22 fresh `npm ci`, lint, verify, production build, focused B03/B07\n105\t  suites plus new controls, full default and controlled test runs separately.\n106\t  Use short synthetic realpath temp roots. Keep original failures and skip\n107\t  reasons, not just the green rerun. No shared node_modules between checkouts.\n108\t- Record source/test SHA inventory and frozen-input preservation. One runnable\n109\t  local commit per feature with feature-id tag, state updated each time.\n110\t\n111\t## F003 compatibility adjudication (2026-10-08)\n112\t\n113\tGenerator reported five unchanged replay-test failures in\n114\t`F003-original-focused.log`: a missing target workspace cwd prevented the worker\n115\titself from starting, incorrectly classifying ordinary Git absence as supervisor\n116\tfailure. Coordinator/Planner approved the following narrow integration repair:\n117\tF003 may also adapt the F001 helper pair so the worker starts from the caller's\n118\tcwd and receives the target child's cwd as a structured argument. Only the\n119\ttarget launch's ordinary ENOENT/non-repository case retains historical absent-Git\n120\tsemantics; helper/protocol failure, timeout and output overflow remain fail-closed.\n121\tAdd distinct target-cwd versus worker-failure controls and rerun the unchanged\n122\tfocused cases. Preserve the first failure log; no historical assertion changes.\n123\t\n124\t## F005: independent acceptance\n125\t\n126\tA fresh Kimi-family evaluator must independently re-derive failure cases from\n127\tthis spec and actual code at the exact committed candidate, not accept Generator\n128\tclaims. Run real resistant-child/descendant/output/deadline probes and verify\n129\towned-process cleanup. Assess all F001-F004 and deliver F005 reports, raw logs,\n130\tschema-valid verdict and a scoped signoff if accepted. Generator cannot perform\n131\tF005. Separate spec-lock critic audits scope and commit-to-feature mapping.\n132\t\n133\tLocal macOS acceptance cannot close native Windows/Linux exact-SHA CI, real\n134\tPG16, browser/F005 of the original homepage batch, release/production gates or\n135\tthe full B03/B07 programme. Explicitly report OS limitations and timing scope:\n136\tstartup budget, operation budget and cleanup allowance are distinct; blocked\n137\tsynchronous filesystem syscalls and adversarial OS suspension are not solved.\n138\tAny FAIL/PARTIAL returns to fixing. Preserve evaluator conclusions verbatim.\n139\t\n140\t## Deferred work and exclusions\n141\t\n142\tRemaining B03 opt-in diagnostics, non-Claude replay adapters, identity migration\n143\tand historical cleanup are not silently enabled here. Diagnostics remain off;\n144\traw upload/retention and destructive migration require separate bounded specs.\n145\tOpenCode mutable-source/cursor consistency is next, followed by B08 CAS,\n146\tB04/B05 release/recovery and the other user-approved packages. No dependency,\n147\tCI workflow, framework, schema, frontend, installer, pricing or capability-version\n148\tchanges in this batch. No unrelated backlog items are consumed."}
